<main class="docs-page">
  <header class="topbar">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">MicuPoker Documentation</p>
      <h1>Play-money Texas Hold'em Simulator &amp; Rules</h1>
    </div>
    <nav>
      <.link navigate={~p"/lobby"}>Lobby</.link>
      <.link navigate={~p"/leaderboard"}>Leaderboard</.link>
      <.link navigate={~p"/"}>Home</.link>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="notice">
    MicuPoker is a complete multiplayer Texas Hold'em poker simulator. Every currency and chip balance on this platform is 100% fictional play money with zero real-world monetary value — no deposits, no withdrawals, no card payments, no cash-out, and no crypto.
  </section>

  <section class="docs-grid">
    <article>
      <h2>Accounts &amp; Guest Seats</h2>
      <p>
        Sit down immediately with an automatic guest identity, or register a permanent username and password account (protected with 210,000-iteration PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA512). Upgrading a guest account preserves your display name, active seats, hand history, and leaderboard stats.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Fictional Currencies &amp; Table Dealer</h2>
      <p>
        Rooms can be created with different fictional play-money currencies (<code>CHIPS</code>, <code>FIC-RON</code>, <code>FIC-EUR</code>, <code>FIC-USD</code>, <code>GOLD</code>, <code>CREDITS</code>, <code>BB-PTS</code>). Each table has a designated
        <strong>Dealer / Host</strong>
        (initially the creator, transferable to any seated player) who can grant fictional funds, adjust or reset stacks, pause/resume dealing, and change blinds or currency between hands.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Simulator HUD &amp; Practice AI Bots</h2>
      <p>
        Seated players receive a live simulator HUD showing estimated hand equity, exact next-street improvement outs, Pot Odds percentage and ratio, Stack-to-Pot Ratio (SPR), and a toggleable Big Blind (<code>BB</code>) stack view. The table dealer can also add or remove practice AI bots (<code>TAG</code>, <code>LAG</code>, <code>GTO</code>, <code>Calling Station</code>) for solo training or short-handed games.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>Private Tables &amp; Card Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        Tables support optional PBKDF2-hashed passwords and spectator controls. The deck is shuffled server-side with <code>:crypto.strong_rand_bytes</code>. Opponent hole cards never leave the server process until an active showdown — folded cards remain hidden even in multi-way showdowns unless the player voluntarily clicks <strong>Show My Cards</strong>.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>WebSocket Protocol</h2>
      <p>
        Endpoint: <code>/socket</code>. Topic: <code>table:&lt;room_id&gt;</code>. Authenticate with the signed
        <code>socket-token</code>
        meta tag via <code>?token=...</code>; raw <code>user_id</code>
        parameters are rejected. Supported events: <code>state</code>, <code>action</code>,
        <code>seat</code>
        (<code>sit_out</code>, <code>sit_in</code>, <code>rebuy</code>, <code>show_cards</code>), <code>react</code>, <code>dealer</code>, and <code>chat</code>.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <h2>HTTP &amp; JSON API Routes</h2>
      <p>
        Read-only JSON endpoints: <code>GET /health</code>, <code>GET /api/rooms</code>, <code>GET /api/rooms/:id</code>, <code>GET /api/stats</code>. Browser routes: <code>/</code>, <code>/lobby</code>, <code>/rooms/:id</code>, <code>/leaderboard</code>, <code>/docs</code>, <code>/login</code>, <code>/register</code>, and <code>/sitemap.xml</code>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</main>
